#~ "publisher; results are automatically filtered to audio-only formats "
#~ "(human/computer narration, audio description, radio drama, DAISY talking "
#~ "books, etc.).\n"
#~ "- Preview any search result before committing to it, or add it straight "
#~ "to a personal library.\n"
#~ "- Multi-part works are handled as a single library entry: playback "
#~ "automatically resumes from the last part and position you left off on, "
#~ "even across NVDA restarts.\n"
#~ "- Play audio books through the same BASS-backed player used for radio and "
#~ "podcasts, with full support for pause/resume, volume, time-shift, "
#~ "playback speed, and output device selection.\n"
#~ "- Download an entire book — all parts, correctly numbered and named — to "
#~ "your recordings folder for offline listening.\n"
#~ "- GETEM sign-in credentials are stored encrypted on disk (Windows Data "
#~ "Protection API) and entered once from FreeRadio's Settings panel.\n"
#~ "- Fixed duplicate/repeated audio in recordings and Time-Shift on HLS "
#~ "streams that rotate session tokens in their segment URLs.\n"
#~ "## Fixed:\n"
#~ "- Cleaned up leftover time-shift buffer files "
#~ "(`freeradio_timeshift_*.buf`) from previous sessions on startup. These "
#~ "are normally deleted when time-shift capture stops cleanly, but an abrupt "
#~ "shutdown (crash, power loss, Windows force-closing NVDA) would skip that "
#~ "step and leave the file in the temp folder — these could accumulate over "
#~ "time, especially with longer buffer durations. The add-on now clears out "
#~ "any matching leftover files each time it starts, before any new capture "
#~ "session begins.\n"
#~ "- Podcast playback speed reverting to normal (1.0x) after switching "
#~ "episodes or resuming from pause. The chosen speed is now resent to the "
#~ "audio engine every time a podcast stream is (re)started, so it stays in "
#~ "effect across episode changes, pause/resume, and station-transition "
#~ "effects (crossfade/tuning) instead of silently resetting.\n"
#~ "## Fixed\n"
#~ "- Fixed a bug where playing a podcast episode could cause a temporary "
#~ "buffer file (`freeradio_timeshift_*.buf` in the system temp folder) to "
#~ "grow to several gigabytes within minutes, potentially filling up the "
#~ "disk.\n"
#~ "  - The time-shift (rewind) capture — designed for continuous live radio "
#~ "streams — was also being started for on-demand podcast/audio book "
#~ "playback. Since those sources can be read far faster than real-time the "
#~ "buffer's time-based trimming couldn't keep up, and each time a chapter "
#~ "finished downloading it was mistaken for a dropped connection and re-"
#~ "downloaded into the same file instead of being cleaned up.\n"
#~ "  - The time-shift buffer is no longer started for podcasts or audio "
#~ "books at all — they already support proper rewind/fast-forward/resume "
#~ "through their own seekable file playback, so nothing is lost.\n"
#~ "  - Live radio time-shift/rewind behavior is unaffected.\n"
#~ "## Fixed\n"
#~ "- **Recording no longer stops when playback changes.** Instant and song-"
#~ "capture\n"
#~ "  recordings were tied to the main player's shared time-shift buffer as "
#~ "an\n"
#~ "  optimisation to avoid capturing a freshly-inserted ad on a brand-new\n"
#~ "  connection. That buffer is a single instance shared by the whole "
#~ "player, so\n"
#~ "  switching stations (or resuming after a long pause) silently cut off "
#~ "any\n"
#~ "  recording that was reading from it. Recordings now always open their "
#~ "own\n"
#~ "  independent connection, so switching stations, pausing/resuming, or\n"
#~ "  stopping playback no longer affects an active recording. The now-"
#~ "unused\n"
#~ "  buffer-tailing code path was removed.\n"
#~ "- **Scheduled recordings no longer report false success.** If a "
#~ "station's\n"
#~ "  stream failed to connect for an entire scheduled recording window, the\n"
#~ "  add-on still announced \"Recording started\" and, at the end, "
#~ "\"Recording\n"
#~ "  finished\" — with no file ever written. A scheduled recording that "
#~ "never\n"
#~ "  connects now reports a failure instead of a false \"finished\" "
#~ "notification.\n"
#~ "## Changed (internal, no functional impact)\n"
#~ "`__init__.py` has been split from a single ~4,200-line file into ten "
#~ "focused\n"
#~ "modules, each ~100–400 lines. `GlobalPlugin` itself is now under 300 "
#~ "lines\n"
#~ "containing only setup/teardown and script routing; everything else is a "
#~ "mixin\n"
#~ "NVDA's script discovery picks up through normal class inheritance, so "
#~ "all\n"
#~ "keyboard shortcuts and default gestures behave exactly as before.\n"
